# Reference-matched cloud studies

Generated using built-in image_gen. Grayscale painted sources on black; not packed textures or coverage masks. Reference: user attachment codex-clipboard-0651474d-986d-443c-8dbd-5d6221e32758.png.

## Cloud 1

Use case: stylized-concept. Create ONE standalone grayscale hand-painted cloud asset matching the attached reference's EXACT painting language: muted medium-gray light planes, deep charcoal shadow valleys, broad overlapping irregular gouache brush shapes with softly feathered transitions and selective crisp broken edges. Strictly grayscale on solid pure black opaque background. No sky, no blue, no cream colors, no text, no border. This is a painted cloud lighting study, NOT a 3D render, NOT photoreal, NOT cotton fluff, NOT smoke tendrils, NOT faceted rocks. Preserve the reference's restrained value range (no brilliant white), thick dark undersides and layered sweeping painted ridges. Make a NEW distinctly different silhouette, not a copy of the reference arrangement. Entire cloud visible with generous black margin. Landscape canvas. Variant 01: tall asymmetrical rising cumulus tower, narrow leaning upper crown and wide low sweeping base, a few small detached fragments. Large and medium masses with painterly interior depth.

